---
{
  "annotations": {
    "destructiveHint": false,
    "idempotentHint": true,
    "openWorldHint": false,
    "readOnlyHint": false
  },
  "description": "Make a model the first layer of a decision, by a revision.\n\nGrades the model as `decision eval --model` does and appends a `Revision` to the decision log only when it meets the evaluation policy, loses no recall, newly fails none of the decision's examples that should pass, and decides a labelled subject the check leaves for review. Otherwise it exits 1 with the reasons and writes nothing; there is no way to force it. The next `check` asks the model first.\n\nExamples:\n  lighthouse model attach design/prefer-method --model local/learned@sha256:3f2a9c1e\n  lighthouse model attach design/prefer-method --model local/learned@sha256:3f2a9c1e --repo cel=../cel\n  lighthouse model attach design/prefer-method --model local/learned@sha256:3f2a9c1e --attributed-to agent:claude --format json",
  "inputSchema": {
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "description": "`model attach`.",
    "properties": {
      "attributedTo": {
        "default": null,
        "description": "Who this is attributed to: `person` or `agent`, with an id after a\ncolon (`agent:claude`). Default: the person from `git config\nuser.name` on the command line, the client's name through MCP.",
        "type": [
          "string",
          "null"
        ]
      },
      "id": {
        "description": "The decision the model judges, such as `design/prefer-method`.",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "labels": {
        "default": null,
        "description": "A table of reviewed findings (`fingerprint repo location verdict`).\nDefault: `plugins/<pack>/labels/<name>.tsv` for the decision `<pack>/<name>`, when it exists.",
        "type": [
          "string",
          "null"
        ]
      },
      "model": {
        "description": "The model to attach, `<provider>/<model>@sha256:<hex>` for a learned\none: graded as the first layer of the decision before anything is\nwritten.",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "repo": {
        "default": [],
        "description": "A repository the labels are about, `name=dir`, where `name` is the\n`repo` column of the table. Repeatable; default: this project.",
        "items": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "type": "array"
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "id",
      "model"
    ],
    "type": "object"
  },
  "name": "model_attach",
  "outputSchema": {
    "$id": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/siyul-park/lighthouse/main/schema/model-attach.schema.json",
    "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
    "description": "What came of asking to attach a model: the `ModelAttach` kind.",
    "properties": {
      "decision": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "evaluation": {
        "description": "The numbers the gate looked at, as a revision records them."
      },
      "model": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "refused": {
        "description": "Why the evaluation does not allow it; none when it was attached.",
        "items": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "type": "array"
      },
      "revision": {
        "description": "The revision that attached it; none when it was refused.",
        "type": [
          "string",
          "null"
        ]
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "decision",
      "model",
      "evaluation"
    ],
    "title": "ModelAttach",
    "type": "object"
  },
  "title": "Make a model the first layer of a decision, by a revision"
}
